\b\fs26 What Hell Harvest does\b0\fs20\par\par
Hell Harvest (formerly Twitch Drops Sentinel) collects Twitch Drops in the background, without the video and without a browser. It includes:\par\par
\li284\fi-284 \u8226?\tab A dashboard and a game queue: priorities, automatic claiming, channel points, a mini window.\par\li0\fi0
\li284\fi-284 \u8226?\tab The Game Shelf: installed games from Steam, Epic and GOG, reward campaigns, the Trophies.md log.\par\li0\fi0
\li284\fi-284 \u8226?\tab Giveaways: free games and assets on Epic Games, GOG, Steam, Fab, Unity, itch.io and Prime Gaming.\par\li0\fi0
\li284\fi-284 \u8226?\tab Steam IDLE: Steam card farming and achievement unlocking.\par\li0\fi0
\li284\fi-284 \u8226?\tab A monitor dimmer, Telegram and Discord notifications, autostart and one-click updates.\par\li0\fi0
\par\par
\b Your data\b0\par
If Hell Harvest or Twitch Drops Sentinel is already installed, setup updates it in place: your settings, account sign-ins and trophy log are kept. If you used an unpacked ZIP, setup offers to bring the data over from the old folder.\par\par
\b Platform rules\b0\par
Automated watching is a grey area of the Twitch Terms of Service. Automating Steam card drops goes against the Steam rules on automated rewards, and unlocking achievements with a program breaks the Steam rules and can lead to restrictions on your account. Automatically claiming free games may also go against the terms of a store. Use it at your own risk.\par\par
Hell Harvest is not affiliated with Twitch, Amazon, Valve or any game store.\par\par
